   214	    - Whenever the ray intersects a pink square, its row or column is mirrored about that square's center line, and the ray continues in the same travel direction from the opposite side of the square.
   215	    - Whenever the ray hits a grey square, it stops and the background cell immediately outside the struck face is colored maroon; if no later square intersects the current ray line, the maroon endpoint is placed on the opposite border cell.
   216	
